<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Baraundha State</h1><p class="st-meta">1549 CE – 1950 CE (approx.) · capital Baraundha</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Raghuvanshi Rajput principality in the hills of Bundelkhand, reputed one of the oldest ruling houses of the region.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The ruling family were Raghuvanshi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajputs</a> who held lands around Patharkachar in the rugged country south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a>, in what became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a>. Their traditional history places the founding of the state in the mid-16th century, but details of its early rulers are sparse.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Baraundha was a small, largely rural state of forest and upland villages ruled by a Raja. After British supremacy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a> in the early 19th century it was confirmed by sanad and supervised through the Bundelkhand and later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rewa-state">Baghelkhand</a> agencies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-india-agency">Central India Agency</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a> its ruler acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and in 1948 Baraundha was merged into the new union of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vindhya-pradesh">Vindhya Pradesh</a>. Its territory now lies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satna-district">Satna district</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/baraundha-state.jpg" alt="Baraundha State" width="320" height="243"><figcaption>Image: John George Bartholomew (1860–1920) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JaitpurKart.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1549 CE – 1950 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Baraundha</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bundeli</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Patharkachar</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1750&amp;focus=baraundha-state" aria-label="Baraundha State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6818 1256 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Baraundha State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7138 1512L7364 1601M7138 1512L7364 1602M7138 1512L7160 1530"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7160 1530h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7138 1512h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7138 1512h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1750&amp;focus=baraundha-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
